  "verbalization": "Hinokiflavone appears to have a relationship with the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex through multiple indirect pathways. The first pathway links Hinokiflavone to DNA polymerase iota, which is subsequently targeted by N-[(4R,10R,13S)-17-[1-(dimethylamino)ethyl]-4-hydroxy-10,13-dimethyl-2,3,4,5,6,7,8,9,11,12,14,15,16,17-tetradecahydro-1H-cyclopenta[a]phenanthren-3-yl]-N,3-dimethylbut-2-enamide, which in turn targets the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. The second pathway connects Hinokiflavone to Phosphodiesterase 6C, which is targeted by Broussoaurone A, which also targets the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. The third pathway links Hinokiflavone to DNA polymerase iota, which is targeted by CID 53630653, which also targets the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. These pathways suggest that Hinokiflavone may act through different molecular intermediates to influence the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. The evidence is consistent but not fully conclusive, as the exact mechanism by which Hinokiflavone interacts with the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex remains to be determined.",
